It happened on it's own while you were 'walking' (flying, actually, 
because you were a winged gargoyle) down the hall because the timeout 
expired.  I think you may be misremembering the message it gave you for 
that.

Several items affect the way the polymorph works.  Amulets of 
unchanging, dragon scale armor, rings of polymorph control, and all 
forms of lycanthropy.

If you wear an amulet of unchanging, you can't change form.  Deaths in 
monster form are permanent.  Polymorph spells, wands, and rings have no 
effect.

If you are wearing dragon armor, you'll poly into that color of dragon, 
breaking out of your cloak and shirt, and merging with the scales until 
the polymorph wears off.  If you poly again in dragon-form, you lose the 
armor.

If you are a werefoo, you'll change back and forth between were and 
<your-race>

If you have poly control, you choose your new form.

If you have none of the above, the RNG rolls a d20, and if it hits 
19-CON or lower, system shock which does 1 to 30 dmg, and you abuse CON. 
  "You shudder for a moment".

If you don't system shock, there's a 1/5 chance that you'll same race 
poly, "You feel like a new man/woman/<race>"

Self polymorph into a monster has a timeout, which can only be held off 
by constantly wearing an amulet of unchanging.  When it times out:
"You return to <race> form!"

The above it paraphrased from the spoilers on Dylan O'Donnell's site, 
